{
  "version": 1,
  "provenance": "Windows package with private-worker Whisper; see docs/security/windows-release-gate.md (MW-SEC-26). The whisper family (runtime/whisper/ Vulkan and runtime/whisper/cpu/, including CPU dispatch variants) is rebuilt from whisper.cpp 371b5a7561823ab2bb32142d2751e35e7534727b staged with scripts/inference/stage-whisper.py (warmup, preview preemption, encoder checkpoints, UTF-8 manifest, runtime/whisper/writer-auth.h private-worker authentication and cpp-httplib 0.58.0 pinned by runtime/whisper/httplib-source.json with pre-authentication limits) and built with scripts/inference/build-windows.py, then assembled by scripts/desktop/replace-windows-speech.py; patch hashes are in notices/writer-whisper-source.txt and configure receipts in notices/whisper-{cpu,vulkan}-*. NeMo-Speech.cpp is not shipped on Windows (Parakeet is unavailable there). The text runtime (runtime/text/cpu and vulkan) is llama-server built from llama.cpp b11393 with miniaudio dc3b628 by scripts/inference/build-windows-text.py (scripts/inference/windows-text-source.json; receipts in notices/text-*). FFmpeg and its notices are byte-identical to the previous package. Never substitute latest upstream binaries. Model weights are excluded. MW-RELEASE-14: the whisper (staged as at 361b181a, the source of the previous bytes), text and FFmpeg runtimes were rebuilt from the same pins with -ffile-prefix-map (scripts/inference/neutral_paths.py) and FFmpeg tools named from PATH, and their receipts/CMake caches copied without home folders, so no build-machine path ships (docs/security/release-personal-paths.md).",
